<title>KUWAIT: Djibouti vessel with Iraqi oil handed to Kuwait.</title>
<headline>Djibouti vessel with Iraqi oil handed to Kuwait.</headline>
<dateline>KUWAIT 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kuwait said on Monday that the international force monitoring a U.N. trade embargo against Iraq had handed over to Kuwait a Djibouti-flagged vessel carrying Iraqi oil.</p>
<p>&quot;The vessel was handed to (Kuwait's) coast guard yesterday (Sunday). It carries Iraqi oil,&quot; said Lieutenant Colonel Adel al-Ibrahim, head of the public affairs department of the Kuwaiti interior ministry.</p>
<p>He said he did not have any further information about the boat.</p>
<p>Iraq has been under stringent United Nations trade sanctions over its 1990 invasion of Kuwait. The sanctions include a ban on the export of oil and import of all commodities expect for food and medicine.</p>
<p>An international naval force monitors compliance with the embargo.</p>
</text>
